      "content": "one thing we're seeing in the prelim testing is that the CDDE can't really handle the nuances of edge-case sensor data like you do. it's just a lot simpler and easier for the auditors to sign off on because it's all binary/deterministic. the goal is basically to move away from anything that isn't a \"yes/no\" rule to avoid any ambiguity in the safety reports.",
